{
  "raw": {
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Athletic-Training_R1005046": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Athletic Training",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description The Department of Kinesiology in the College for Community Health at Montclair State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Athletic Training, beginning August 27, 2027. We seek a faculty member whose teaching, research, and professional engagement advance the field of Athletic Training and contribute to the preparation of future healthcare professionals. Areas of expertise may include, but are not limited to, injury prevention, clinical biomechanics, rehabilitation, therapeutic interventions, sport and human performance, emergency care, health and wellness, or other areas relevant to Athletic Training education and practice. The successful candidate will contribute to creating an engaging and supportive learning environment for the undergraduate and graduate programs in Athletic Training and Kinesiology and play an important role in preparing students for professional practice through classroom, laboratory, and clinical education experiences. Applicants should demonstrate potential for impactful scholarship, excellence in teaching, and a commitment to student mentorship and success. The ability to engage in interdisciplinary collaboration, interprofessional education, and community-engaged scholarship is highly desirable. As part of the College for Community Health, the successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with faculty across health-related disciplines and contribute to initiatives that promote health, wellness, and quality of life in diverse populations. In addition, the candidate is expected to contribute to service activities at the department, college, and university levels; maintain an active scholarly agenda; support accreditation and program assessment activities; and engage with healthcare, athletic, educational, and community partners throughout the region. The successful candidate will join a collaborative department committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service, with access to the extensive healthcare, sport, and professional opportunities available throughout the New York metropolitan area. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching : The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release. THE DEPARTMENT OF KINESIOLOGY The Department of Kinesiology at Montclair State University is dedicated to preparing future leaders in athletic training, physical education, exercise science, sport administration, coaching, and related professions through innovative undergraduate and graduate education. The department advances the University’s mission by educating highly skilled professionals, fostering scholarship and community engagement, and developing partnerships that address workforce needs across healthcare, educational, sport, and corporate settings. Through nationally recognized and accredited programs, including a CAATE-accredited Athletic Training program, hands-on clinical and experiential learning opportunities, and a commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and service, the department prepares graduates to improve health, safety, physical activity, athletic performance, and quality of life in diverse communities. Faculty are committed to student success, interdisciplinary collaboration, and advancing evidence-based practice across the health, sport, and performance professions. THE COLLEGE FOR COMMUNITY HEALTH The College for Community Health (CCHL) at Montclair State University is dedicated to addressing pressing health inequities in New Jersey, the region, and beyond. We are dedicated to furthering the Montclair State University mission by educating and preparing students to meet the needs of the health workforce; engaging with communities and the public to improve health services, systems, and outcomes, and developing meaningful inquiry and scholarship in and for health. In synergy with existing groups and organizations, leveraging the university's strengths, and expanding academic offerings to meet critical health workforce needs, CCHL is leading the way to healthier people and communities, establishing itself as a key transformational leader in the New Jersey region and beyond. CCHL faculty are committed to interprofessional education and student engagement, with three priority areas: maternal and child health, wellness, and healthy aging across our 7 academic departments.           QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree (or ABD with degree completed by date of appointment) in Athletic Training, Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Rehabilitation Sciences, Health Sciences, or a closely related field. Board of Certification (BOC) credential in good standing as a Certified Athletic Trainer. Eligibility for licensure as an Athletic Trainer in the State of New Jersey. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED: Significant record of scholarly/creative work. Previous teaching experience in an Athletic Training program or related health professions with special interest in CAATE-accredited experience, clinical education, preceptor development, and student supervision. Experience integrating simulation, technology, or innovative instructional methods into teaching. Expertise in one or more areas such as: Injury prevention Rehabilitation and therapeutic interventions Clinical biomechanics Emergency care (including BLS CPR/AED instructor certification) Sport performance Manual therapy Health promotion and wellness Healthcare administration Athletic Training pedagogy Evidence of interdisciplinary or interprofessional collaboration. Demonstrated ability or potential to develop partnerships with healthcare systems, secondary schools, collegiate athletics programs, or other clinical sites. Demonstrated ability to foster an inclusive learning environment that supports student success. Interest in securing external funding and contributing to community-engaged scholarship, service, or collaborative research initiatives. Previous experience with program assessment, accreditation, or curriculum development.            STARTING DATE                August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process. Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately.   APPLY BY:   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $69,373.45-$108,433.95 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Kinesiology Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Workday-Technical-Developer_R1005067": {
      "title": "Workday Technical Developer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Manager of Integrations, the Workday Technical Developer supports and enhances our Workday environment, specifically in Finance, Human Capital Management (HCM), and Student modules. This role focuses on leveraging Workday’s advanced technical capabilities, including Workday Reports, Extend, Prism Analytics, AI, and Integrations (including Enterprise Interface Builders, or EIBs). This role is instrumental in maintaining the efficient operation and ongoing enhancement of our Workday system, ensuring it meets organizational requirements and supports data-driven decision-making. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Customize and configure Workday applications to meet our organizations requirements. Develop Workday Extend. Coordinate and support Workday Integrations including Core Connectors, Studio, and EIBs. Develop, implement, and maintain Workday PRISM Analytics solutions to provide comprehensive data insights and support decision-making processes. Assist in the optimization and usage of AI. Provide system and end user support and guidance. Troubleshoot and test Workday applications to ensure a strong day-to-day operation. Properly document applications and integrations. Create and maintain reports. Provide findings, progress updates, and recommendations as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in Information Technology, Computer Science, Business, or related field. Minimum four (4) years of professional experience in a Workday Technical Developer role or similar position with direct experience in Finance, HCM, or Student modules. Demonstrated experience with Workday Integrations, including Core Connectors, Workday Studio, and EIBs. Proven ability to work with Workday Extend, Prism Analytics, and AI functionalities. PREFERRED : Master’s degree from an accredited university in Information Technology, Computer Science, Business, or related field. Experience working for a Higher Education institution. Familiarity with Workday security roles, domain policies, and business processes. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instruction. Salary Range $97,624.85-$126,919.75 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Integration Development Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Teaching-Professor_R1005064": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description POSITION DESCRIPTION: The Feliciano School of Business at Montclair State University invites applications for a two-year renewable, full-time non-tenure-track Business Statistics faculty position starting September 1, 2027. Ideal candidates for this position will have both professional experience in industry and teaching experience at the university level. Preference for this position will be given to candidates who can demonstrate teaching/professional experience in Business Statistics. The candidate selected will be expected to teach courses at undergraduate and graduate levels in both face-to-face and online delivery modes. Position is a two-year, ten-month, non-tenure track appointment, with eligibility for reappointment based on established NTTP procedures. Teaching Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching and service. Teaching: The standard annual teaching load for 10-month teaching faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with an additional 6 TCH in the summer for 12-month faculty. Reassigned time (course release) is available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as administering programs. Teaching Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Service: Teaching Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, and university. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which teaching faculty members receive course release. THE DEPARTMENT OF INFORMATION MANAGEMENT AND BUSINESS ANALYTICS: The Department of Information Management & Business Analytics offers a BS in Business Analytics and a BS in Business Administration with concentrations in Management Information Systems, a minor in Business Analytics, and MS in Business Analytics. The department also supports the MBA Program, teaching both required (core and concentration-specific) and elective graduate courses. THE FELICIANO SCHOOL OF BUSINESS The Feliciano School of Business is committed to transforming today’s students into tomorrow’s business leaders through innovative teaching, experiential learning, and strong industry engagement. Accredited by AACSB International, the School offers distinctive programs at both the undergraduate and graduate programs, including the BS in Business Analytics, BS in Business Administration (eight concentrations), BS in Accounting, BA in Economics, BA in Hospitality, Sports, Events and Tourism, MBA, MS in Accounting, MS in Business Analytics, MS in Digital Marketing Analytics, and MS in Human Resource Analytics, as well as a range of minors and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Among the School’s strengths are its world-class faculty and staff, diverse and driven student body, engaged alumni network, and strong corporate and institutional partnerships. Both academic and program-related activities are focused on student success and experiential learning beyond the classroom. The Ellyn A. McColgan Center for Student Services further supports students through results-driven advising, career guidance, and access to internships, co-ops, and mentorship opportunities that help prepare them for success in today’s dynamic business environment. The School is also home to the Feliciano Center for Entrepreneurship + Innovation, a collaborative community that supports innovation and entrepreneurship through mentorship, strategic guidance, and opportunities that help students and entrepreneurs develop and grow their ideas. Nearly 120 full-time faculty members and 41 professional staff, with terminal degrees and advanced training from leading universities, bring a wealth of academic and industry expertise to the School. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: ● Master’s degree in statistics, business analytics, data science or a related field ● Demonstrated or potential excellence in teaching business statistics. ● Practical experience in applied statistics, business analytics or related field. ● A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. STARTING DATE August 27, 2027 REQUIRED MATERIALS: ● Cover letter, curriculum vitae and teaching and service statements which can be uploaded during the application process. ● Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. APPLY BY: The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $99,127.91-$99,127.91 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Information Management and Business Analytics Position Type Teaching Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Teaching-Professor--Health-Psychology_R1005038": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Health Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description DEPARTMENT/SCHOOL/COLLEGE : Department of Psychology/School of Behavioral and Cognitive Sciences/College of Humanities and Social Sciences/School POSITION DESCRIPTION:  The Department of Psychology at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time, 10-month, non-tenure track, Assistant Teaching Professor position in Health Psychology, beginning in August 2027. We seek a dynamic and collaborative colleague whose expertise in Health Psychology will contribute to a coordinated departmental initiative to expand Health Psychology across undergraduate, graduate, and online programs. This position represents an exciting opportunity to join one of the largest psychology departments in the region and to play a central role in building a distinctive Health Psychology presence that integrates research, education, and community impact. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Health Psychology and related areas and will serve as a key contributor to the development, assessment, and improvement of Health Psychology curricula and programs. The position offers opportunities to collaborate with faculty on innovative instructional initiatives, experiential learning opportunities, and community partnerships that enhance student success and career readiness. The Department of Psychology values an inclusive, student-centered academic environment, and seeks colleagues who demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in teaching, mentorship, and advising, as well as a dedication to engaging and supporting a diverse student population.  The position is a two-year, ten-month, non-tenure track (NTT) appointment, with eligibility for reappointment based on established NTT procedures. Montclair is committed to the success of teaching faculty through opportunities for promotion and professional development to support long-term success and flourishing at the University.  Teaching Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching and service. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for 10-month teaching faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with an additional 6 TCH in the summer for 12-month faculty.  Additional TCH reassigned time (course release) is available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as administering programs. Teaching Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Service : Teaching Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which teaching faculty members receive course release. DEPARTMENT OF PSYCHOLOGY The Psychology Department—organized into the three broad categories of clinical, industrial/organizational (I/O), and psychological science—serves a large and diverse constituency of students, and comprises a vibrant group of 35 full-time faculty, in addition to several emeriti faculty and support staff. The Department continues to expand its national profile, with 20 active research labs, over 3.5 million dollars in extramural funding, and PhD programs in both clinical and I/O psychology—in addition to popular MA and certification programs in clinical psychology, I/O psychology, psychological science, and advanced quantitative methods. The research interests of our faculty include neuroscience, neurodegenerative diseases, and neurocognitive aging; cognitive processes such as memory, the brain reward system, decision-making, perceptual processing, and spatial cognition; internalizing psychological disorders and trauma; forensic investigation, plea bargaining, and forensic and correctional assessment and treatment; language and life span development; motivation; pedagogy; effective leadership, mentorship, and supervision; organizational behavior; employee well-being, aging, and longevity; emotions and ethics in the workplace; and social attitudes, discrimination, diversity science, and social justice. COLLEGE OF HUMANITIES AND SOCIAL SCIENCES The College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS) is Montclair State’s largest college, with over 5,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students. CHSS facilitates traditional and interdisciplinary learning and is the professional home of many outstanding scholars and instructors across numerous disciplines, all of whom lend to CHSS’s mission to furnish academically rigorous and relevant programs of study that contribute to the development of an informed and engaged civil society. CHSS’s programs develop in students the abilities to discover, create, evaluate, apply, and share knowledge, so that they will be able to think critically, act ethically, and be informed citizen-participants prepared to assume leadership roles in their communities. CHSS also aims to be responsive to the needs of society, including via its championing of use-inspired research collaboratively undertaken by faculty and students, and graduate programs that train students to apply knowledge in constructive, inspiring, and practical ways that benefit our local and broader communities. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Earned PhD in Psychology Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED : Preferred candidates will have a PhD in health psychology or a closely related subfield, with demonstrated excellence in teaching. We are open to subareas of specialization, and welcome candidates whose work addresses contemporary challenges in health and well-being, including behavioral health, chronic disease management, health equity, prevention science, aging, stress and resilience, digital health, and social determinants of health. Consideration will also be given to candidates who complement existing Department strengths in clinical psychology and I/O psychology.    STARTING DATE       August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae and teaching and service statements which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. Questions about the search can be addressed to Dr. John Paul Wilson: wilsonjoh@montclair.edu   APPLY BY :    The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $66,067.40-$95,821.86 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Psychology Position Type Teaching Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Health-Psychology_R1005050": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Health Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description DEPARTMENT/SCHOOL/COLLEGE : Department of Psychology/School of Behavioral and Cognitive Sciences/College of Humanities and Social Sciences POSITION DESCRIPTION:  The Department of Psychology at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty position in Health Psychology beginning in August 2027. We seek a dynamic and collaborative colleague whose expertise in Health Psychology will contribute to a coordinated departmental initiative to expand Health Psychology across undergraduate, graduate, and online programs. This position represents an exciting opportunity to join one of the largest psychology departments in the region and to play a central role in building a distinctive Health Psychology presence that integrates research, education, and community impact. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate instruction in their area of expertise and maintain an active and productive research program. Responsibilities include publishing in high-quality scholarly journals, pursuing external funding opportunities, mentoring student researchers, and contributing to the department's growing national reputation for research excellence. The Department of Psychology values an inclusive, student-centered academic environment and seeks colleagues who are committed to excellence in teaching and mentorship, as well as to engaging and supporting a diverse student population. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with additional TCH reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities.  . Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. . Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release.  THE DEPARTMENT OF PSYCHOLOGY  The Psychology Department—organized into the three broad categories of clinical, industrial/organizational (I/O), and psychological science—serves a large and diverse constituency of students, and comprises a vibrant group of 35 full-time faculty, in addition to several emeriti faculty and support staff. The Department continues to expand its national profile, with 20 active research labs, over 3.5 million dollars in extramural funding, and PhD programs in both clinical and I/O psychology—in addition to popular MA and certification programs in clinical psychology, I/O psychology, psychological science, and advanced quantitative methods. The research interests of our faculty include neuroscience, neurodegenerative diseases, and neurocognitive aging; cognitive processes such as memory, the brain reward system, decision-making, perceptual processing, and spatial cognition; internalizing psychological disorders and trauma; forensic investigation, plea bargaining, and forensic and correctional assessment and treatment; language and life span development; motivation; pedagogy; effective leadership, mentorship, and supervision; organizational behavior; employee well-being, aging, and longevity; emotions and ethics in the workplace; and social attitudes, discrimination, diversity science, and social justice. THE COLLEGE OF HUMANITIES AND SOCIAL SCIENCES The College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS) is Montclair State’s largest college, with over 5,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students. CHSS facilitates traditional and interdisciplinary learning and is the professional home of many outstanding scholars and instructors across numerous disciplines, all of whom lend to CHSS’s mission to furnish academically rigorous and relevant programs of study that contribute to the development of an informed and engaged civil society. CHSS’s programs develop in students the abilities to discover, create, evaluate, apply, and share knowledge, so that they will be able to think critically, act ethically, and be informed citizen-participants prepared to assume leadership roles in their communities. CHSS also aims to be responsive to the needs of society, including via its championing of use-inspired research collaboratively undertaken by faculty and students, and graduate programs that train students to apply knowledge in constructive, inspiring, and practical ways that benefit our local and broader communities. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Earned PhD in Psychology Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED Preferred candidates will have a PhD in health psychology or a closely related subfield, with demonstrated excellence in teaching. We are open to subareas of specialization, and welcome candidates whose work addresses contemporary challenges in health and well-being, including behavioral health, chronic disease management, health equity, prevention science, aging, stress and resilience, digital health, and social determinants of health. Consideration will also be given to candidates who complement existing Department strengths in clinical psychology and I/O psychology.  Significant record of scholarly/creative work.  STARTING DATE      August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply three letters of recommendation separately. Questions about the search can be addressed to Dr. John Paul Wilson: wilsonjoh@montclair.edu .   APPLY BY:     The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately.   Salary Range $76,486.40-$100,398.29 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Psychology Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Criminal-Justice_R1005049": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Criminal Justice",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description DEPARTMENT/SCHOOL/COLLEGE : Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies/School of Social Sciences/College of Humanities and Social Sciences POSITION DESCRIPTION:  The Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies at Montclair State University is actively seeking applications for an Assistant Professor in Criminal Justice to begin in August 2027. For this tenure-track appointment, we are engaging in a broad search in any area of criminal justice or criminology, however, we are particularly searching for professors ready to offer courses in our required sequence, including research methods, criminology, and/or the department’s interdisciplinary course on theories of justice. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with additional TCH reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities.  . Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. . Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release.  THE DEPARTMENT OF SOCIOLOGY, CRIMINOLOGY, AND JUSTICE STUDIES:  The Department of Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies is the second largest department in the College of Humanities and Social Sciences.  Our criminal justice concentration alone has over five hundred enrolled majors.  We also offer a master’s degree in Justice Innovation and Leadership.  Featuring dynamic faculty from a variety of disciplines, our interdisciplinary focus includes Criminal Justice/Criminology, Law, International Justice, and Social Justice. Justice Studies serves a large minoritized and first generation college student population. Our faculty are dedicated to providing support and guidance for our students, as well as a robust education experience to prepare them for the workforce. THE COLLEGE OF HUMANITIES AND SOCIAL SCIENCES:  The College of Humanities and Social Sciences (CHSS) is Montclair State’s largest college, with over 5,000 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students. CHSS facilitates traditional and interdisciplinary learning and is the professional home of many outstanding scholars and instructors across numerous disciplines, all of whom lend to CHSS’s mission to furnish academically rigorous and relevant programs of study that contribute to the development of an informed and engaged civil society. CHSS’s programs develop in students the abilities to discover, create, evaluate, apply, and share knowledge, so that they will be able to think critically, act ethically, and be informed citizen-participants prepared to assume leadership roles in their communities. CHSS also aims to be responsive to the needs of society, including via its championing of use-inspired research collaboratively undertaken by faculty and students, and graduate programs that train students to apply knowledge in constructive, inspiring, and practical ways that benefit our local and broader communities. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, Sociology, or a related field. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED Significant record of scholarly/creative work.  Experience teaching criminology, criminal justice, or sociology courses at the undergraduate level. Experience teaching a diverse student body and first generation college students. Peer-reviewed publications in criminology, criminal justice, or a related field. STARTING DATE      August 27, 2027      REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process.  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately.   APPLY BY :   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $76,486.40-$100,398.29 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
