    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor--Management_R1005054": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Management",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description POSITION DESCRIPTION : The Feliciano School of Business at Montclair State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Organizational Change and the Future of Work , starting on August 27, 2027. The Department of Management seeks a scholar whose research and teaching examines how organizations anticipate, lead, and adapt to major changes in work, technology, structure, and talent systems, including topics such as organizational change, change leadership, the future of work, digital transformation, AI in organizations, workforce analytics, and human-technology collaboration.   The successful candidate will contribute to both undergraduate and graduate programs in management, entrepreneurship, human resources, and project management, and play a key role in developing innovative, future-focused courses such as Organizational Change and Development, Future of Work, Digital Transformation and Change Leadership, Leadership in Technology-Enabled Organizations, Human and AI Collaboration, and Workforce Analytics.  Scholarly focus and agenda should include organizational change, the future of work, digital transformation, AI in organizations, workforce analytics, or related technology-enabled changes in management. The ability to engage in interdisciplinary collaboration and community-engaged scholarship is also highly desirable. Teaching : The standard annual teaching load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with additional TCH reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release. DEPARTMENT DESCRIPTION: The Department of Management is a dynamic and growing unit within the Feliciano School of Business. With strengths in strategy, entrepreneurship, organizational behavior, and HR, the department is committed to preparing students for leadership in a rapidly evolving business environment. The Management curriculum emphasizes innovation, collaboration, and the application of theory to real-world challenges. The department offers a BS in Business Administration with concentrations in Management, Entrepreneurship, and Strategic Human Capital Management, a minor in Entrepreneurship, two graduate certificate programs in Human Resources Management and Project Management, as well as three undergraduate certificate programs in Entrepreneurship, Innovation Design, and Neuroinclusive Practice and Leadership. The department also supports the MBA Program and the MS in Human Resources Analytics program, teaching both required (core and concentration-specific) and elective graduate courses. Enrollment in management programs has strengthened in recent years as students increasingly seek coursework in leadership, organizational change, technology, analytics, and the future of work. The department supports this interest through new program development, strong industry partnerships, and faculty who blend scholarly rigor with practical relevance. SCHOOL DESCRIPTION The Feliciano School of Business is committed to transforming today’s students into tomorrow’s business leaders through innovative teaching, experiential learning, and strong industry engagement. Accredited by AACSB International, the School offers distinctive programs at both the undergraduate and graduate programs, including the BS in Business Analytics, BS in Business Administration (eight concentrations), BS in Accounting, BA in Economics, BA in Hospitality, Sports, Events and Tourism, MBA, MS in Accounting, MS in Business Analytics, MS in Digital Marketing Analytics, and MS in Human Resource Analytics, as well as a range of minors and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Among the School’s strengths are its world-class faculty and staff, diverse and driven student body, engaged alumni network, and strong corporate and institutional partnerships. Both academic and program-related activities are focused on student success and experiential learning beyond the classroom. The Ellyn A. McColgan Center for Student Services further supports students through results-driven advising, career guidance, and access to internships, co-ops, and mentorship opportunities that help prepare them for success in today’s dynamic business environment. The School is also home to the Feliciano Center for Entrepreneurship + Innovation, a collaborative community that supports innovation and entrepreneurship through mentorship, strategic guidance, and opportunities that help students and entrepreneurs develop and grow their ideas. Nearly 120 full-time faculty members and 41 professional staff, with terminal degrees and advanced training from leading universities, bring a wealth of academic and industry expertise to the School.   QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Earned doctorate or appropriate terminal degree. Record of achievement and potential for future success in research, scholarship or creative activity. Demonstrated excellence in teaching all students. A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED Significant record of scholarly publications. A PhD in Management, I/O Psychology, Organizational Behavior, Strategy, Human Resource Management, or a closely related discipline is required by the start date. Research agenda that addresses organizational change, the future of work, digital transformation, AI in organizations, workforce analytics, or related technology-enabled changes in management. Evidence of or potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate levels. STARTING DATE         August 27, 2027 (Pending confirmation from the Registrar’s Office)     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications, which can be uploaded during the application process. Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. APPLY BY:   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $130,000.00-$160,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Management Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Director-of-Technology-Strategy---Innovation_R1004960": {
      "title": "Director of Technology Strategy & Innovation",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Dean of the Feliciano School of Business, the Director of Technology Strategy & Innovation provides strategic leadership for the planning, advancement, and effective use of technology across the School. The Director develops and executes technology strategies that support excellence in teaching, learning, research, student success, administration, and external engagement while ensuring that technology capabilities evolve to meet the changing needs of students, faculty, and staff. The Director identifies and evaluates emerging technologies, promotes innovation, and advances technology-enabled solutions that strengthen the School's academic and operational effectiveness. As a member of the Dean's senior leadership team, the Director serves as the School's principal advisor on technology strategy, digital transformation, artificial intelligence, data and analytics, and technology investments. The Director collaborates with University technology partners, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders to advance technology initiatives aligned with the School's mission and strategic priorities while overseeing the delivery of technology support services within the School. The Director also represents the School in institutional technology initiatives and maintains active engagement with peer and aspirant business schools to identify and advance best practices in technology-enabled education and operations. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop and execute a comprehensive technology roadmap aligned with the School's strategic priorities, ensuring effective resource planning, measurable outcomes, and a culture of innovation and continuous improvement. Serve as the School's senior advisor on technology strategy, digital transformation, artificial intelligence, and emerging technologies, providing recommendations to the Dean and senior leadership regarding opportunities, risks, investments, and adoption strategies. Partner with the Dean, senior leadership, faculty, and staff to integrate technology into academic, administrative, and strategic initiatives that advance teaching, learning, research, student success, and operational effectiveness. Evaluate existing and emerging technologies through the use of business intelligence, data analytics, cost-benefit analysis, and risk assessment to inform technology planning and investment decisions. Lead technology modernization and digital transformation initiatives across academic delivery, student services, and administrative operations, applying effective project and change management practices to support successful implementation and adoption. Partner with faculty to advance the effective use of educational technologies, artificial intelligence, analytics, and other emerging technologies within curriculum design, instructional delivery, experiential learning, and student success initiatives. Promote the effective use of data analytics, dashboards, and business intelligence tools to support decision-making, program assessment, operational effectiveness, and student outcome tracking. Represent the School in University technology initiatives, committees, and working groups, advocating for School priorities while contributing to institution-wide technology planning and innovation efforts. Develop and maintain relationships with peer and aspirant business schools, professional organizations, and industry partners to identify emerging trends, share best practices, and support technology-enabled learning opportunities. Serve as the School's representative in the development and implementation of University policies and initiatives related to artificial intelligence, data governance, cybersecurity, and technology innovation. Promote cybersecurity awareness and support the implementation of University information security, privacy, and compliance requirements within the School, working closely with central technology and security units. Lead the direction and continuous improvement of School technology support services, including instructional design and educational technology, workstation support, virtual desktop environments, audiovisual services, and media production. Oversee the daily operation of the SBUS Technology Support Services unit, including personnel management, budget administration, service delivery, assessment, and compliance with University policies and procedures. Provide strategic recommendations regarding technology investments and collaborate with University technology and procurement units on the acquisition and implementation of hardware, software, and cloud-based services supporting School priorities. Oversee the reliability, effectiveness, and continuous improvement of School-managed technology resources, including computer labs, virtual desktop environments, instructional technology systems, and end-user computing resources. Monitor technology utilization, service performance, and operational metrics and provide periodic assessments and recommendations to the Dean regarding technology effectiveness, resource allocation, and future priorities. Supervise, mentor, and develop a team of technology professionals responsible for instructional technology, educational technology support, workstation services, audiovisual support, virtual desktop environments, and media production. Maintain sufficient operational knowledge to ensure leadership continuity and effective service delivery during periods of organizational transition, staffing changes, or increased operational demand. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution in information technology, information systems, computer science, analytics, business technology, or a related field. Minimum of seven years of progressively responsible experience in technology, digital transformation, information systems, analytics initiatives, or related functions within a complex organization. Minimum of five years of experience leading professional staff, managing complex projects, and overseeing technology-related operations or initiatives. Demonstrated knowledge of artificial intelligence, generative AI, and emerging technologies, with the ability to evaluate opportunities, risks, and translate complex technical concepts into practical recommendations for diverse stakeholders. Experience using data analytics, business intelligence, reporting, or assessment tools to support strategic planning, decision-making, and organizational effectiveness. Demonstrated success leading multiple concurrent projects and organizational change initiatives, including technology adoption efforts in complex environments. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with senior leaders, faculty, staff, students, and external stakeholders and to build collaborative relationships across organizational boundaries. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, matrixed environment and manage competing priorities. Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to balance strategic objectives and operational needs.   PREFERRED: Master's degree (MBA with a concentration in Information Systems, Analytics, Technology Management, or a related field; or a master's degree in Information Systems, Information Technology, Analytics, Computer Science, or a related discipline) from an accredited institution. Advanced professional certifications in project management, artificial intelligence, information technology leadership, cybersecurity, cloud technologies, analytics, or related fields. Demonstrated experience leading AI strategy, AI governance, responsible AI adoption, or emerging technology initiatives within a complex organization. Demonstrated success leading technology modernization, digital transformation, organizational change, or large-scale process improvement initiatives. Experience supporting technology-enabled teaching and learning, educational technology, instructional innovation, or digital learning initiatives. Experience developing or leveraging analytics, dashboards, business intelligence, or data-informed decision-making processes to support organizational strategy and performance. Experience leading technology initiatives within higher education or similarly complex, mission-driven organizations operating in collaborative and shared-governance environments. Familiarity with cybersecurity frameworks, data privacy requirements, and technology governance practices relevant to higher education environments. Experience developing partnerships with corporations, technology providers, professional organizations, or other external stakeholders that support experiential learning, workforce development, innovation, or curriculum enhancement. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $165,000.00-$185,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Feliciano School of Business Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Associate-Director-of-Residential-Education_R1005044": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Residential Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the Director of Residential Education, the Associate Director of Residential Education is responsible for coordinating all activities, programs, as well as training, selection and development for all student staff lines for the Department. The Department is responsible for more than 5,500 students residing in various apartment and residential communities on two campuses, including two complexes maintained through a joint effort with Capstone On Campus Management. The Associate Director of Residential Education collaborates with University Campus partners to assist in the creation of a seamless residential experience for residents. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: ● Supervise the Residential Student Support Specialist and Graduate Program Coordinator, and indirect oversight of 330 student employees. ● Lead student staff hiring, training, and development for all academic year and summer student staff positions. ● Develop and implement learning objectives, manuals, and training programs for student staff positions. ● Coordinate logistics for training events, speakers, and development activities. ● Oversee recruitment processes including interview design, scoring rubrics, and hiring workflows. ● Maintain the student staff roster and manage onboarding in collaboration with Human Resources. ● Evaluate performance of student staff through structured tools. ● Support student governance, including Residence Hall Associations and councils in collaboration with Assistant Directors and live-on professional staff. ● Collaborate with campus partners to enhance the residential living experience. ● Develop, monitor and evaluate the residential curriculum and make annual improvements. ● Support Assistant Directors and Graduate Program Coordinator in compiling programming metrics and reports. ● Maintain programming inventory and recommend long-term supply purchases. ● Create promotional materials and maintain proficiency in relevant software tools. ● Lead department co-sponsorship initiatives and other programming in partnership with campus offices. ● Assist with residence hall opening/closing, special events, and weekend programming as needed. ● Serve as on-call administrator for residential life emergencies. ● Represent the department on inter- and intra-departmental committees. ● Demonstrate professional ethics, initiative, and engagement in departmental meetings. ● Management retains the right to change or add job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS: REQUIRED: ● Masters degree from accredited college or university in higher education administration, student personnel services or related field. ● A minimum of six years of professional residence life or student affairs experience with a record of progressive advancement and supervision. ● Excellent time management skills plus a strong proficiency in written and oral communication. ● Direct experience with professional and student staff supervision, training and development, residence hall activities and educational programs. PREFERRED: ● Experience working with multicultural groups. ● Live-in experience. ● Knowledge of college student development, programmatic needs, and fostering a sense of belonging. ● Working knowledge of project management methodologies and a desire to improve efficiency, quality, and customer satisfaction with a focus on continuous improvement. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instruction. Salary Range $87,500.00-$88,580.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Residential Life Education Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Shuttle-Supervisor--Weekend-_R1004981": {
      "title": "Shuttle Supervisor (Weekend)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Director of Transportation Services, the Shuttle Supervisor is responsible for field supervision of transportation operations and the daily execution of bus service between the Montclair and Bloomfield campuses.  The Shuttle Supervisor is additionally responsible for direct oversight and evaluation of transportation drivers. The Supervisor also monitors personnel and equipment to assist in the coordination of service and schedules, ensures compliance with safety procedures and confers with customers or supervising personnel to address questions, problems, or requests for service or equipment. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES :  Supervise transportation work operations, plan work assignments and bus allocations to meet operational goals of the department. Monitor personnel to coordinate optimum utilization of service and schedules. Dispatch drivers to appropriate routes, demand-response, and special events. Supervises bus drivers in the field and monitors GPS systems so that passengers are transported according to schedule. Maintain communications with drivers throughout shift; managing telephone or radio reports regarding delays, equipment breakdowns, accidents, and other operating difficulties. Take necessary steps to resolve difficulties, coordinate replacement equipment or staff to restore service. Prepare appropriate paperwork when necessary. Assist and implement safety procedures in compliance with local, state and federal rules/regulations including Department of Transportation (DOT). Make temporary adjustments to schedules and routes as required to meet passenger demand. Ensure that drivers perform pre- and post-trip inspections and bring vehicles into garage for regular scheduled maintenance. Review, analyze, and interpret applicable federal and/or state laws and regulations affecting the unit. Ensure that drivers adhere to University Human Resources, DOT, FTA, and departmental requirements. Supervise and evaluate subordinate employee performance through the review of assigned work as well as through university-wide Performance Assessment Review. Establish and maintain liaison and cooperative working relationships with college administrators, faculty, staff, students, student organizations, government and private agencies, and/or the public to accomplish the objectives of the unit. Ensure that any accidents or other incidents are properly reported, notifying appropriate units such as University Police. Participate in the formation of policies and procedures. Assist in the development, evaluation and upgrading of safety programs. Coordinate and/or assist with orientation of new drivers. Assist in preparation of bi-weekly payroll in Workday. Participate in Drug and Alcohol testing as required by the University and applicable federal and/or state laws. Coordinate bus repairs with Fleet Services to ensure equipment is maintained and ready for service. Demonstrate continuous effort to improve operations, decrease turnaround times, streamline work processes, and work cooperatively to provide quality customer service. Drive buses to cover demand when necessary and as directed. Supervise subordinates in a fair and equitable manner. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED :  Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Minimum of three (3) years of supervisory experience overseeing bus, shuttle service or transportation operations. Driving privileges with good standing in the state of New Jersey with Commercial Driver’s License Class A or B with passenger endorsement. Ability to read, write, speak and understand English sufficiently to perform the duties of the position. Successful candidates must be flexible and available to be assigned to any shift, overtime, and holidays with adequate notice. PREFERRED : Familiarity with Microsoft Office. Ability to establish cooperative working relationships with offices or organizations that impact on or relate to work of Shuttle Services. *NOTE: This is a Civil Service position.  As required by the State of New Jersey, in order to be certified to the position and attain permanent status in title, candidates are required to successfully serve a 4-Month Working Test Period. This position is designated as essential. The designation of essential requires employees at these 24/7 facilities to be present due to inclement weather situations. This position requires on campus work and is not a position that allows remote work.        SALARY RANGE: R24: $76,286.63 - $111,856.03 * NOTE : Salaries for internal candidates are determined by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission’s formula. Salaries for external candidates are determined up to step four, $86,957.45.   NJ SAME Applicants This position is a non-competitive, unclassified posting and complies with the NJ SAME Program. If you are applying under the New Jersey \"SAME\" program, your supporting documents (Schedule A or B letter), resume (CV), as well as the names and contact information for three professional references should also be sent to: same@montclair.edu and hrcompliance@montclair.edu For more information on the SAME program visit their website at: https://nj.gov/csc/same/overview/index.shtml , email: SAME@csc.nj.gov , or call CSC at: 833-691-0404. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act P.L. 2011 c.70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees in certain positions (other than faculty who are exempt) are required to obtain New Jersey residency within one (1) year of employment. Applicants who have a concern with meeting this requirement should discuss with Human Resources if the position for which they have applied is eligible for an exemption from this requirement. Salary Range $76,286.63-$86,957.45 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department TRANSPORTATION SERVICES Position Type Support Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/BAS-HVAC-Automations-Technician_R1005056": {
      "title": "BAS/HVAC Automations Technician",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Director of Mechanical Maintenance, the BAS/HVAC Automations Technician provides high-level technical expertise in the operation, maintenance, troubleshooting, repair, and installation of heating, ventilation, air conditioning (HVAC), and building automation systems (BAS). This position monitors and advances the uninterrupted operation of building environmental controls, and ensures that systems operate efficiently, safely, and in compliance with applicable codes and standards. This position requires both hands-on technical expertise and oversight of staff work and system operations. The incumbent is expected to actively engage in troubleshooting and system optimization.   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES :  Oversee the operation and maintenance of: heating and cooling systems air handling units, rooftop units, and distribution systems motors and controls hydronic systems including pumps, valves, and piping building automation systems (BAS) and associated controls Monitor and troubleshoot BAS controls to ensure proper system performance, energy efficiency, and occupant comfort. Diagnose complex HVAC and control issues and direct appropriate corrective actions. Coordinate preventive maintenance programs for HVAC and control systems. Review system alarms, trends, and performance data to identify deficiencies and implement improvements. Oversee calibration, programming, and troubleshooting of control systems and field devices. When directed, supervise, assign, and review the work of HVAC mechanics, controls technicians, and related staff engaged in maintenance and repair activities. When directed, coordinate work with contractors and vendors performing specialized HVAC and controls services. Assist in planning, scheduling, and executing system upgrades, retrofits, and capital improvement projects. Ensure compliance with applicable codes, standards, and safety regulations. Maintain records of maintenance activities, system performance, and equipment history. Estimate labor, materials, and equipment required for maintenance and repair work. Respond to emergency situations involving HVAC or building control systems. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED :  Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in a mechanical or electrical field. Minimum  three years of experience in HVAC maintenance, troubleshooting, repair, or installation work. HVAC or Refrigeration Certification.Building Automation Systems training or Certification. A valid driver’s license.   PREFERRED : Minimum five years of experience in HVAC maintenance, troubleshooting, repair or installation work. Experience with electromechanical and electrical controls, VFD programming and installation. Experience with computerized building automation systems. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.   Salary Range $76,486.40-$95,599.98 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department STEM Mechanical Services Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Senior-Accountant_R1004858": {
      "title": "Senior Accountant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY :  Reporting to the Director of General Accounting, the Senior Accountant is responsible for ensuring accurate general ledger account balances that are substantiated by the completion of monthly account analysis and reconciliations and timely close of the University's financial records. This position is also responsible for accounting of fixed assets, construction in progress and leases under GASB 87 guidance. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES :   Prepare complex general ledger account reconciliations and detailed analysis of assigned general ledger accounts. Prepare bank reconciliations. Review and monitor account activity to ensure accuracy, completeness, and the proper recording of transactions. Research and resolve discrepancies and prepare appropriate journal entries as required. Assist in close procedures and month end close process by completing steps as assigned. Perform accounting for Fixed Assets, construction in progress, capital projects and leases under GASB87 guidance. Work collaboratively with Finance & Treasury associates and other University departments to ensure that deposit/disbursements are recorded in the system in the period of occurrence. Identify and recommend improvements to financial controls and reporting; implement approved changes to existing processes. Prepare audit schedules and footnotes; assist with audit inquiries. Actively participate in or lead special projects as assigned including testing system implementations, upgrades, or enhancement; conducting financial analysis and developing ad hoc reports; and processing improvement initiatives.   Meet deliverable deadlines. Assist stakeholders and requestor so they understand account balances and content. Answer account and other financial questions by researching and interpreting data. Assist the Financial Reporting area in understanding account balances by providing account fluctuation explanations. Resolve helpdesk tickets as first level support for general ledger inquiries. Provide end user training/guidance in one on one and group settings. Keep abreast of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) as issued by the Government Accounting Standards Board (GASB) and the Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB) as well as of State and Federal circulars and Internal Revenue Service rules and regulations. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS :  REQUIRED :   Bachelor's degree in accounting from an accredited university or college. Minimum of five years of relevant experience in a financial/accounting function preparing account analysis, reconciliations and fixed assets. Knowledge and experience with journal entries, financial statement preparation, and general accounting concepts including GAAP and application as issued by GASB and/or FASB. Excellent customer service. Ability to maintain confidentiality. PREFERRED :  Experience with Workday or a similar ERP system. CPA or CPA eligible. Advanced Excel skills, including pivot tables. Experience working for a higher education institution, a large nonprofit organization. Experience in data mining. Team player with strong communication skills. Decision making, problem solving and troubleshooting skills. Professional demeanor. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $80,000.00-$90,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department General Accounting and Financial Reporting Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Professor-of-Biology--Biomedical-Science_R1005051": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology, Biomedical Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description The Department of Biology at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor in Biomedical Science . We seek an outstanding scholar and educator who will establish an innovative, externally funded research program involving undergraduate and graduate students, demonstrate excellence in teaching across the biology curriculum, and contribute to the department's strong tradition of collegiality, service, and student success. The successful candidate will join a dynamic and collaborative department within a growing R2 institution committed to inclusive excellence, interdisciplinary research, and innovation in science education. Teaching could include courses in introductory cell and molecular biology, advanced molecular biology, genetics, or courses in other areas developed by the successful candidate. These courses will support graduate and undergraduate students in the biology degree program tracks.   All research areas in cell and molecular biology will be considered, with a preferred emphasis on biomedical research using both standard and innovative organismal models. We seek candidates who are interdisciplinary, collaborative, and student-centric. As a Biology Department that integrates the work of ecology, physiology, and cell/molecular researchers, we welcome multidisciplinary research approaches. The involvement of undergraduate and graduate students in research is a priority, including a mentoring approach providing fundamental training in the process of science. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching :   The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities.    Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the department, college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release.  DEPARTMENT OF BIOLOGY The Department of Biology at Montclair State University is a leader in authentic, research-driven learning experiences, providing students with hands-on opportunities to explore biological sciences from molecular biology to ecosystems biology. We maintain a unique balance between providing a small-school feel while educating a large, diverse student body through a strong emphasis on excellent teaching and mentoring, supported by a team of professional advisors dedicated to student success. The department fosters a collaborative culture among its 24 faculty members, supporting interdisciplinary research and teaching innovation. Innovative initiatives include the SEA-PHAGES program, a Howard Hughes Medical Institute-supported project that enables students to conduct authentic research on soil-borne viruses from their first year. Students benefit from field-based learning opportunities that extend from the local environment of New Jersey to locations as far as the Galapagos. Cutting-edge laboratory courses integrate the latest technologies, allowing students to address real-world biological questions. The department is actively developing interdisciplinary degree programs, including a new BA in Biology and collaborations in Neuroscience and Biotechnology to ensure that our graduates develop a deep understanding of biological systems and current scientific methods, and adopt a critical-thinking mindset that will prepare them for diverse career pathways. We are deeply committed to fostering an environment that supports success for all students and to creating a community where staff, faculty, and students feel welcome. The Department of Biology works closely with the Health Careers Program, offering pathways for students to thrive in health-related fields. We prioritize creating a welcoming and supportive community where every student can succeed.  THE COLLEGE OF SCIENCE AND MATHEMATICS The College of Science and Mathematics at Montclair State University empowers the next generation of STEM leaders through rigorous academics, hands-on discovery, and inclusive excellence. Our mission is grounded in a student-centered philosophy that values the dedication of our faculty, the curiosity of our students, and a shared commitment to advancing scientific knowledge and innovation. With modern facilities and cutting-edge technology, we offer distinctive undergraduate and graduate programs across the Departments of Biology, Chemistry and Biochemistry, Earth and Environmental Studies, Mathematics, and Physics and Astronomy, and the School of Computing. Through a research-driven curriculum, community-engaged learning, and real-world problem-solving experiences, CSAM equips students with durable skill sets to meet the demands of an evolving world. By cultivating strong partnerships with industry, government, and nonprofit organizations, the College drives economic growth, advances environmental sustainability, and strengthens the STEM workforce across New Jersey and beyond. QUALIFICATIONS A Ph.D. in molecular biology, cell biology, or a related biomedical field. Demonstrated excellence in teaching is required, as evidenced by peer/student evaluations and/or other materials, particularly in appropriate specialty and introductory-level biology courses. A track record of recent research publications is required, along with a history of successful grant activity. SALARY RANGE      Commensurate with experience     STARTING DATE     August 27, 2027     REQUIRED MATERIALS:  -Cover letter   -Teaching statement   -Research statement   -Curriculum vitae -Representative publications or working papers (combined into a single file) -Names and contact information of three professional references  Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply three letters of recommendation. APPLY BY:   The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately. Salary Range $80,309.12-$116,469.62 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Biology Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Independent-Rater--Temp--Grow-NJ-Kids_R1005047": {
      "title": "Independent Rater (Temp) Grow NJ Kids",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description Summary The Independent Raters facilitate and score classroom observations in early care and education programs (i.e., child care centers, preschools, home-based family care), using the ECERS-3, ITERS-3, and/or FCCERS-3 observation protocols. Independent Rater (Temp) positions report to the Grow NJ Kids Classroom Observation Coordinator at CREEHS. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Establish and maintain reliability on ECERS-3, ITERS-3, and/or FCCERS-3 classroom observation scales Participate in all required project training Schedule visits with early care and education (ECE) center-based, school-based, and/or home-based family care programs Conduct classroom observations at ECE program sites in a professional and confidential manner Score classroom observation scales, and share observation data and program feedback with CREEHS Maintain communication with CREEHS project team Perform other duties as assigned Hours Temporary position, up to 25 hours per week Note that classroom observations typically take place Monday through Friday between 8 am - 12 pm (plus travel time) Qualifications Required Minimum of a Child Development Associate (CDA) credential or an Associate degree in early childhood education or a related field 1 or more years of professional experience in ECE settings Demonstrated familiarity with Environmental Rating Scales (ECERS-3, ITERS-3, FCCERS-3) Valid Driver's License Ability to travel throughout NJ, including driving to program sites statewide as needed (mileage and tolls to be reimbursed) Preferred Spanish fluency Previously established reliability with Environmental Rating Scales (ECERS-3, ITERS-3, FCCERS-3) Bachelor's degree in early childhood education or a related field Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strengths both as a team player and a self-starter Strong organizational and time management skills Demonstrated ability to work effectively in a team and with diverse populations PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $30.00-$35.00 Hourly The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department CREEHS 15 (Temporary) Position Type Hourly - Temporary Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Senior-Producer_R1004935": {
      "title": "Executive Producer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the News Director, the Executive Producer is responsible for NJ PBS's news content across all platforms, including broadcast programs, digital content, live streaming, and live coverage. This position plans and executes the daily news broadcasts that air on NJ PBS, including a weeknight evening newscast, a weekday news interview talk show, and any special broadcast coverage of planned events or breaking news. This position also oversees the planning and editorial direction of content on digital platforms and live streaming channels.  The Executive Producer works closely with the News Director to balance breaking news (on digital and/or linear platforms) with planned coverage.   PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Build and manage the daily rundown and oversee the live production of video-based news programs — including those for the nightly newscast and other broadcast programs, digital platforms, and special event coverage — selecting and ordering stories for maximum editorial impact. Time scripts and segments to appropriate length depending on platform.  Coordinate with the assignment desk, reporters, anchors, and technical staff to ensure all elements are ready before they are posted or aired.  Write and edit scripts and promos for daily programs. Assist in developing future NJ PBS live-streaming channels. Track story progress and production deadlines, alerting producers, reporters,  and editors when deadlines are at risk.  Adapt coverage plans in response to breaking news, re-stacking rundowns and coordinating live coverage as needed. Review reporter packages and edited content before it is posted or aired, checking for accuracy, fairness, and technical quality. Oversee the planning and execution of news content on all digital platforms. Supervise the Producer, Digital Content; the V-Mix Operator; and the Graphics Producer and Editor to ensure seamless content delivery across broadcast, digital, and live streaming platforms.   Work closely with the News Director to develop coverage strategies, establish editorial priorities, and ensure consistency across NJ PBS news platforms. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. ​ QUALIFICATIONS :  REQUIRED: A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in journalism, communications, broadcasting, or a related field.  Minimum of four years of experience in broadcast news production, including rundown management, live newscast and special event program execution. Demonstrated experience in digital news content production on multiple platforms. Proficiency with newsroom management systems and broadcast production tools. Ability to work under deadline pressure in a fast-paced live news environment. Strong background in journalism. PREFERRED: Experience at a news media organization or PBS-affiliated station. Familiarity with the New Jersey news landscape Experience with digital-first and multiplatform newscast workflows Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $95,000.00-$120,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Medical-Assistant-Student-Health-Center--Temporary-_R1005025": {
      "title": "Medical Assistant Student Health Center (Temporary)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description Reporting to the Director of University Health Services, the Student Health Center Medical Assistant is responsible for providing direct patient care in accordance with the Student Health Center’s standards. The Medical Assistant will work alongside our team members to assist with both administrative and clinical duties. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Responsible for maintaining patient flow. Monitor for patient’s arrival, accompany and/or assist patients into the exam room. Obtain patient vital signs and transcribe to patient medical record in a timely fashion. Report abnormal vital signs to APN immediately. Perform a variety of diagnostic CLIA waived point of care testing. Collect and process lab specimens. Maintain point of care testing logs Assist healthcare providers during examinations and procedures as needed. Perform venipuncture procedure in accordance with clinical standards. Restock, clean and prepare medical exam rooms and lab. Perform other related duties as assigned. Management retains the right to change or add job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS :  REQUIRED :   Completion of a formal medical assistant training program (NHA, NCCT, AMT, AAMA, NCMA, AMCA, AECA, or NAHP) Current CPR/AED certification High school diploma PREFERRED :  6 months experience in a primary care setting preferred Experience working with young adults and diverse populations, including LGBTQ+ patients PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $20.00-$23.00 Hourly The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Health Center (Temporary) Position Type Hourly - Temporary Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/vMix-Operator_R1004943": {
      "title": "vMix Operator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to Senior Producer, the vMix Operator is the technical production engine for NJ PBS, responsible for the direction, assembly, and delivery of the daily video-based news segments, shows, and original programming. Operating a single-operator vMix production environment, this position directs and assembles pre-recorded and live content, executes graphics and audio, and delivers broadcast-ready program files to the central playout hub and PBS master control. This is not a traditional multi-position control room role — it requires a uniquely versatile operator equally fluent in technical production, editorial workflow, and digital distribution, who takes full ownership of on-air quality from first frame to final delivery. This on-site position is based at NJ PBS production facilities at Montclair State University.  PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Serve as sole technical director and operator for the daily Monday–Friday newscast, working within a pre-recorded, late-afternoon assembly workflow. Build and manage show rundowns in coordination with the editorial team; ingest, log, and organize all story packages, reporter tracks, and anchor footage. Assemble the complete newscast in vMix, executing graphics, lower thirds, full-screen elements, video playback, transitions, and audio mixing in a single-operator environment. Ensure all segments meet broadcast quality standards for video levels, audio normalization (LKFS/R128), closed captioning integration, and format compliance. Encode and deliver the finished program to the central playout hub by established daily deadline, using required file formats and delivery protocols. Monitor and troubleshoot delivery pipelines; escalate technical failures immediately and maintain backup delivery procedures. Assemble original NJ PBS programs, specials, and documentary content using the vMix environment. Coordinate with producers and editors on post-production workflows, ensuring compatibility between editing systems and vMix playout. Manage multi-source productions including remote contributors via NDI, IP video, or other streaming inputs. Build and maintain vMix project templates for recurring show formats to ensure consistency and production efficiency. Operate and manage the graphics workflow within vMix, including integration with character generator tools and external design assets. Encode and distribute content for streaming platforms, social media, and the NJ PBS owned-and-operated digital hub. Assist in the configuration and maintenance of live streaming workflows for breaking news, special events, and digital-first content. Serve as the primary operator and day-to-day steward of the vMix production system; Work with engineering and IT dept to maintain software licensing, updates, and hardware performance. Work with engineers to troubleshoot and resolve technical issues with cameras, audio systems, monitors, signal routing, and network infrastructure. Collaborate with IT and engineering staff on systems maintenance, upgrades, and redundancy planning. Document production workflows, technical configurations, and delivery specifications for organizational continuity. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time.     . QUALIFICATIONS:  REQUIRED: Associate’s or Bachelor’s degree in Broadcasting, Communications, Film/Video Production, or a related field, or equivalent professional experience. Minimum three years of experience in broadcast television production, with demonstrated experience in a technical director or production operator role. Hands-on proficiency with vMix software; ability to build and execute complex productions as a single operator. Strong understanding of broadcast signal flow, video formats (HD/4K), audio standards (PCM, LKFS/R128), and delivery file specifications. Experience with newscast production workflows, including rundown management, package ingest, and deadline-driven delivery. Working knowledge of broadcast graphics systems; ability to operate and update graphics packages. Familiarity with closed captioning integration and FCC compliance requirements. Ability to work independently under deadline pressure with minimal supervision. PREFERRED: Experience with NDI-based IP video workflows and remote production. Familiarity with PBS technical standards, delivery requirements, and affiliate operations. Experience encoding and publishing content for OTT, streaming, and social platforms. Background in public media, journalism, or news production environments. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud (Premiere Pro, After Effects, Photoshop) or equivalent; video editing experience strongly preferred. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.  Salary Range $80,000.00-$90,000.00 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Open-Rank-Tenure-Track-Faculty-Position--Collaborative-Keyboard_R1005030": {
      "title": "Open Rank Tenure Track Faculty Position, Collaborative Keyboard",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description POSITION DESCRIPTION: The John J. Cali School of Music at Montclair State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Collaborative Keyboard at the open rank. We seek an accomplished and imaginative artist-educator who will contribute equally through excellent teaching and mentorship, an active program of performance and creative or scholarly inquiry, and collaborative leadership within the School. The successful candidate will join a vibrant, student-centered community in which performers, educators, composers, scholars, therapists, producers, and creative partners work across disciplines to advance artistic excellence and prepare students for meaningful, adaptable careers in music. This position offers an opportunity to shape the future of collaborative keyboard at the Cali School while maintaining an active professional profile and developing innovative learning and performance opportunities for undergraduate and graduate students. Faculty members are expected to contribute to the University's mission through excellence in teaching, research/scholarship, and service. Teaching : The successful candidate will teach and coach undergraduate and graduate students in areas aligned with their expertise and the needs of the School. In addition to offering Keyboard area courses, responsibilities may include chamber music coaching, vocal coaching for opera and musical theatre, private keyboard instruction, and collaboration with vocal and instrumental ensembles. The faculty member will advise and mentor students, support recruitment and auditions, and foster an inclusive learning environment that develops versatile, collaborative, and professionally prepared musicians. In addition, the successful candidate will provide artistic and administrative leadership for collaborative keyboard activities across the Cali School. Responsibilities may include coordinating collaborative assignments, contributing to curriculum and program development, supporting instructional faculty and collaborative artists, strengthening concerts and interdisciplinary projects, and helping to develop equitable and sustainable processes for the School’s extensive performance activities. The standard annual load for tenure-track faculty is 12 teaching credit hours (TCH) a semester, with reassigned time (course release) available for faculty with additional responsibilities such as mentoring doctoral faculty or administering programs. Faculty are expected to center student success and measurable learning outcomes through clear course design, inclusive pedagogies, and the integration of emerging disciplinary and pedagogical developments. Responsibilities include classroom instruction, student mentoring and advising, and developing and updating courses and curricula aligned with student demands and institutional strategic priorities. Research, Scholarship, and Creative Activity : Faculty are expected to be productive scholars or artists whose work embodies formal inquiry or creative expression that expands, enhances, or applies knowledge. Research results must be shared in significant national and/or international scholarly or artistic venues following rigorous review. The University supports these endeavors through the Faculty Scholarship Program (FSP), which typically provides research-active faculty with up to 6 TCH of reassigned time per academic year to pursue their scholarly agenda. The successful candidate will maintain an active program of performance, research, and creative or scholarly activity appropriate to a tenure-track appointment. This work may include collaborative performance, recording, coaching, interdisciplinary projects, residencies, conference presentations, publications, or other forms of artistic and intellectual contribution. The faculty member will be encouraged to connect professional practice with student learning and to build collaborations across the School, University, and broader cultural community. Service : Faculty members are expected to perform valuable service to the college/school, university, and professional communities. This includes participating in shared governance, academic program vitality, and sharing professional expertise within and beyond the University. Service activities are separate and distinct from the specific assignments for which faculty members receive course release. THE JOHN J. CALI SCHOOL OF MUSIC: The John J. Cali School of Music offers undergraduate and graduate degrees in music education, music performance, music therapy, theory/composition, jazz studies, and recording arts and production, as well as a two-year Artist's Diploma and one-year Performer's Certificate. The Cali School collaborates with the Theater and Dance Department to provide voice instruction for students in the nationally recognized BFA Musical Theater program. Twenty-one full-time faculty members (fourteen of whom are tenured) and approximately 200 part-time instructors serve more than 500 students, who matriculate through a competitive admissions process. The school maintains strong relationships with professional performance and educational organizations along with several music schools around the world, and in the 21-22 Academic Year launched two major new initiatives with the Cali Pathways Project, focused on reducing barriers for burgeoning musicians in under-resourced communities, and the Cali Immersive Residency program, embedding world-renowned artists and ensembles for week-long residencies at the school. Its facilities provide a conservatory-like setting, consisting of the 235-seat Jed Leshowitz Recital Hall, teaching studios, music practice and rehearsal rooms, and faculty studios. Our students and faculty engage in over 300 concerts and recitals each year. THE COLLEGE OF THE ARTS: The College of the Arts (CART) at Montclair State University is a dynamic, collaborative, and inspiring community. With more than 40 undergraduate and graduate programs across the Department of Art & Design, the John J. Cali School of Music, and the Department of Theatre and Dance, CART is a vibrant hub of creativity and innovation. Over 2,000 diverse and talented students bring our state-of-the-art studios, stages, and classrooms to life every day, supported by passionate academic advisors and a career services team dedicated to their success. Programs are rigorous, creative, and designed to meet the needs of all students while offering rich opportunities for experiential learning, performance, and internships. Our faculty is a powerhouse of working composers, designers, actors, musicians, choreographers, conductors, fine artists, scholars, and professionals – Fulbright, Guggenheim, and Howard Award recipients among them – who shape the next generation through close mentorship and hands-on learning. The College is also home to the University Art Galleries, Arts and Cultural Programming, and Broadcast and Media Operations, anchoring deep connections with corporate and arts partners. Whether on campus or in the broader community, CART pulses with energy, excellence, and the belief that the arts can transform lives. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: ●    Earned appropriate terminal degree in music or a related field, or possess equivalent distinguished professional experience. ●    Record of achievement and/or potential for future success in research, scholarship, or creative activity. ●    Demonstrated excellence in teaching a broad range of students. ●    Demonstrated professional achievement and/or potential in collaborative performance. ●    A record that demonstrates interest and commitment to service. PREFERRED: ●    Significant record of scholarly/creative work with clear potential for a distinguished career as a performing artist, educator, and/or scholar at both national and international levels ●    Strong background in program development, including student recruitment, concert planning, and artistic leadership ●    Experience working across a variety of musical disciplines and genres. ●    Proficiency in lyric diction in several languages. ●    Strong artistic, organizational, and interpersonal skills. STARTING DATE: August 27, 2027    REQUIRED MATERIALS: ●    Cover letter, curriculum vitae, research and teaching statements, and representative publications where applicable (publications may include commercial recordings, concert programs, and/or scholarly books and articles), which can be uploaded during the application process. ●    Links to recent recordings of at least two collaborative performances, rehearsals, masterclasses, or other relevant collaborative activity. ●    Candidates who are shortlisted will be asked to supply 3 letters of recommendation separately. APPLY BY:    The position is open until filled, and application review begins immediately.  Applications received by October 16, 2026 will receive priority consideration. Questions may be addressed to the search chair, Prof. Aaron Helgeson, at helgesona@montclair.edu. Salary Range $80,309.12-$136,463.80 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Cali School of Music Position Type Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Director-of-Major-and-Planned-Giving_R1005035": {
      "title": "Director of Major and Planned Giving",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-13\nPosted: Posted 23 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Assistant Vice President of Major and Planned Gifts, the Director of Major and Planned Giving is a key leader within the University Development team who advances the university’s mission and strategic priorities through transformational philanthropy. The Director identifies, cultivates, solicits, and stewards individuals capable of making major and planned gifts, and works to grow the planned giving program through estate and other deferred-giving vehicles. The Director leads strategies to engage high-net-worth individuals and advances comprehensive giving efforts aligned with the institution’s long-term strategic goals. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES :  Build and manage a portfolio of 100–125 high-capacity prospects with the potential to make major gifts of $50,000 or more, providing stewardship that reflects best practices in donor relations. Identify, qualify, and engage new major and planned giving prospects, with particular emphasis on non-alumni and high-net-worth individuals, by mobilizing new networks.  Conduct face-to-face meetings with prospects, including travel as necessary. In partnership with the Assistant Vice President of Major and Planned Gifts, identify and articulate compelling gift proposals for affiliated and unaffiliated prospects. Develop creative, persistent and personalized outreach strategies to new philanthropic individuals and entities aligned with the university’s strategic plan and campaign priorities. Prepare compelling briefing materials, proposals, and gift agreements to support solicitations. Coordinate major and planned giving activities across schools and departments to ensure alignment with university priorities. Guide the narrative, data, and storytelling behind major and planned giving proposals in partnership with the Assistant Vice President of Major and Planned Gifts. Direct research efforts to qualify new affiliated and unaffiliated prospects’ philanthropic interests and giving capacity. Monitor significant philanthropic investment announcements and emerging trends in higher education philanthropy. Assist in the planning and direction of high-level donor engagement events. Support the development and expansion of the planned giving program to grow long-term philanthropic support through bequests, trusts, beneficiary designations, and other deferred giving vehicles. Serve as one of the institution’s in-house experts on charitable estate planning and complex gift structures. Oversee the administration of estate gifts, working with legal counsel, executors, and the university foundation to ensure timely and accurate realization of bequests. Design and implement marketing and outreach plans to promote planned giving opportunities, including digital campaigns, direct mail, seminars, and legacy society initiatives. Steward existing planned giving donors and oversee the administration and recognition of realized estate gifts. Partner with major gift officers to identify and promote blended gift opportunities. Provide training and guidance to development colleagues on identifying planned giving prospects and integrating gift planning discussions into broader donor conversations. Engage university leadership, trustees, and volunteers in promoting planned giving initiatives. Manage and grow the university’s legacy society, ensuring appropriate recognition, engagement, and stewardship of planned giving donors. Monitor and report on program metrics and results, and maintain accurate records of planned gifts for leadership, development staff, and volunteers. Partner with development colleagues, university administrators, faculty, and the university foundation to maximize donor engagement and secure significant commitments. Represent the university at donor events, board meetings, regional alumni gatherings, and community functions. Draft high-level correspondence, proposals, impact reports, and stewardship materials tailored to principal and planned giving donors. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED :  Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Minimum of seven years of progressively responsible experience in major gift fundraising, planned giving, or a related development role, ideally within higher education or a large nonprofit institution. Demonstrated success personally soliciting and closing major gifts of $50,000 or more. Proven experience structuring and closing planned/deferred gifts such as bequests, charitable trusts, gift annuities, and beneficiary designations. Track record of building and managing a high-capacity prospect portfolio of 100 or more prospects. Working knowledge of tax law, estate planning principles, and charitable gift vehicles, including bequests, charitable remainder and lead trusts, gift annuities, retained life estates, and beneficiary designations. Strong strategic thinking and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple complex initiatives simultaneously. High emotional intelligence and a donor-centered approach to relationship building. Persuasive written and verbal communication and presentation skills, including comfort presenting to high-net-worth individuals, boards, and volunteers. Collaborative, team-oriented leadership style with the ability to influence without direct authority. Proficiency with donor database and CRM systems (e.g., Blackbaud, Ellucian, Salesforce) and prospect research tools. Sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential donor and financial information. Ability to travel regularly, including some evenings and weekends, for donor meetings and events. Commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in donor engagement and team collaboration. PREFERRED : Advanced degree, or coursework/certification in gift planning, nonprofit management, law, or a related field. Experience partnering with legal counsel, financial advisors, or estate administrators on complex gift arrangements. Experience developing and leading marketing or outreach campaigns for a legacy society or planned giving program. Supervisory or mentoring experience, including training frontline fundraisers on gift planning conversations. Chartered Advisor in Philanthropy (CAP®) or Certified Fund Raising Executive (CFRE) certification. Active membership or participation in the National Association of Charitable Gift Planners (CGP) or a similar professional association. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $115,000.00-$125,000.00 Annual The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Major Gifts and Development Leadership Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Enrollment-Coordinator--Per-Diem----Graduate-Business-Programs_R1005036": {
      "title": "Enrollment Coordinator (Per Diem) – Graduate Business Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 24 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description Montclair State University’s Feliciano School of Business is seeking an Enrollment Coordinator (Per Diem) to support graduate business programs, including MBA, Analytics and Accounting Programs. The coordinator will work closely with the Graduate Admissions office to provide critical support across student onboarding, enrollment management and retention. The ideal candidate is organized, detail- and data-oriented, and enjoys working with prospective and admitted students. The outline below highlights primary duties; additional responsibilities may be assigned. Key Responsibilities Student Support and Advice Provide guidance on program sequencing, course options, and scheduling logistics for prospective and newly admitted students. Advise prospective 4+1 students to discuss program eligibility and options Manage and update 4+1 programs pipeline documents to onboard students   Information Sessions & Event Management Plan, schedule, and present content during in-person and virtual information sessions. Track attendance, follow-up with participants, and assist with conversion to enrollment. Support recruitment events, executive speaker series, and new student orientations.   Student Onboarding & Registration Support Assist newly admitted students through orientation and first-semester registration. Code students appropriately in student systems and coordinate with advisors and the registrar to resolve registration issues. Enrollment Monitoring & Reporting Monitor new student course enrollments  Present program enrollment outlook reports and analyze data Assist with classroom space planning and course capacity management Generate combined bachelor’s to master’s (4 +1) student reports and monitor and communicate with students in the pipeline Student Engagement & Retention Support Support student progress and retention in programs  through proactive outreach, communication, and retention initiatives. Collaborate with faculty, advisors, and staff to connect students with appropriate resources and support services.   Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree One year of experience in higher education, student services, recruitment, or advising Strong organizational and communication skills Ability to manage multiple tasks, deadlines, and priorities independently Familiarity with student information systems and CRM tools preferred Professional demeanor and ability to interact with students, faculty, and staff Up to 35 hours per week, Monday-Friday. Flexibility will be required for occasional evening or weekend events. Preferred Qualifications Experience with graduate business programs or recruitment Knowledge of course registration, enrollment reporting, and onboarding processes Comfortable presenting at information sessions or events Application Instructions Apply through Workday with a resume and cover letter detailing relevant experience PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions. Salary Range $23.00-$26.00 Hourly The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department MBA Program (Temporary) Position Type Hourly - Temporary Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
