    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Employer-Relations-Specialist--College-of-Science-and-Mathematics-_R1005017": {
      "title": "Employer Relations Specialist (College of Science and Mathematics)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the Director of Career Services in the College of Science and Mathematics (CSAM), the Employer Relations Specialist will develop and implement employer engagement strategies, cultivate employer partnerships, and coordinate and secure resources to support career-related programs that expand student access to internships, cooperative education, and career opportunities. Success in this role requires independent judgment, strong collaboration skills, attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple priorities from inception to completion. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and implement employer engagement strategies aligned with college and institutional priorities. Build, manage, and strategically grow relationships with employer partners to expand and sustain pipelines for internships, cooperative education, and career opportunities. Conduct employer site visits to deepen partnerships and increase experiential learning opportunities. Partner with employers to design branding and marketing strategies that maximize student engagement. Design, plan, and execute employer engagement programs and events, including career fairs, networking events, and site visits, with responsibility for outcomes and continuous improvement. Operate with a high level of independence and accountability, exercising professional judgment while collaborating with stakeholders and leadership to advance unit and institutional goals. Collaborate with CSAM departments and university career services staff to align employer engagement efforts across colleges/schools. Analyze employer engagement metrics, student participation, and program outcomes to inform strategy, improve effectiveness, and guide decision-making. Maintain current knowledge of workforce and industry trends, particularly within science and mathematics fields. Ensure events are executed with strong attention to detail from planning through post-event assessment. Review, approve, and manage job postings in Handshake. Leverage platforms such as Handshake, LinkedIn, and Montclair Connect to promote opportunities and engage stakeholders. Lead and contribute to marketing and communication strategies that promote employer partnerships and student engagement. Uphold university policies related to employer engagement and student services, including FERPA. Represent the department at university events and serve on committees as appropriate. Perform other duties as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: Master's degree from accredited college or university in higher education, counseling, career services, business, science, and mathematics-related fields, or a closely related discipline. Minimum of three years of experience in career services, employer relations, recruitment, or event coordination. Demonstrated ability to build and sustain strategic relationships with employers and external partners. Strong communication, interpersonal, and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively across all organizational levels. Proven ability to manage multiple priorities and independently coordinate complex initiatives, including employer engagement and large-scale events. Proficiency in career services platforms and technology tools (e.g., Handshake, LinkedIn, Zoom, Microsoft Office, Google Workspace). Experience utilizing data to inform outreach strategies, assess program effectiveness, and support continuous improvement. Ability to collaborate effectively across departments and with external partners. Flexibility to support occasional evening and weekend programming. PREFERRED: Experience developing and implementing employer engagement strategies in a higher education setting, particularly with STEM-focused organizations. Experience analyzing recruitment, engagement, or program data to inform decision-making and improve outcomes. Familiarity with science and mathematics career pathways and experiential learning opportunities (internships, cooperative education, research placements). PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.   Salary Range $76,486.40-$87,954.55 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department CSAM Career Services Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assistant-Director--Assignments-and-Operations--Office-of-Residence-Life-_R1004830-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Assignments and Operations (Office of Residence Life)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Director of Housing Operations and Logistics, in the Office of Residence Life, the Assistant Director, Assignments and Operations oversees the operational and systems-based functions of housing assignments and occupancy management for the residence halls. Working closely with departmental and campus partners, the position manages room assignments, cancellations, waitlists, move-in/move-out processes, and summer housing operations to support maximum occupancy and a seamless residential experience. The role serves as a key liaison for housing software, policies, reporting, and communications, including marketing, web presence, and student messaging, while ensuring consistent application of housing policies and supporting major departmental events and emergency coverage.  PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Collaborate with the Director on occupancy planning and modelling for each academic year based on the needs/requirements of the University. Ensure maximum occupancy by generating, running and reviewing daily reports and completing appropriate follow-through actions with staff members. Utilize and maintain proficiency in housing software to manage day-to-day assignments, room changes, vacancies and reassignments, and provide professional, customer service-oriented responses to students and parents with housing issues. Manage the cancellation process for residence hall housing agreement releases. Design and produce data driven reports for the department of Residence Life that identify key metrics to support strategic decision making. Evaluate and appropriately recommend system enhancements and functionality within the Housing Software, including the development and implementation of all policies, procedures and training for staff related to housing software and communication. Interpret and communicate procedures and regulations pertaining to housing policies to ensure consistent application of these policies throughout the department. Grow and develop marketing strategies to promote housing accommodations using social media and communication channels available at the University. Design and implement all housing assignment processes for new and returning students, including the management of compliance requirements for all residential students. Work in conjunction with the Disability Resource Centre on resident student accommodations. Partner with other campus partners to prepare the Red Hawk Central for opening. Oversee and manage the operations required for all move-ins and move-outs, including residents, summer programs, and conferences with the Housing Operations team in collaboration with Residence Education. Serve as the primary liaison between the Office of Residence Life and the Office of Student Communications, ensuring clear, timely, and effective communication between both units. Develop, design, and maintain the Office of Residence Life website, as well as create and manage the social media, email, and marketing content. Participate in the Manager on Call duty rotations to support residential operations and student needs after standard business hours. Represent the Office of Residence Life at key university programs and events such as Open House, Admission events, and Welcome Week. Perform other related duties as assigned. Management retains the right to change or add job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED:  Master’s degree from an accredited university in Student Personnel, Student Affairs, Higher Education, Administration or related field.  Minimum of two years of professional Residential Life experience within higher education or a related field. PREFERRED: Previous experience with residential life room assignments, including day-to-day response to room changes, vacancies and reassignment of rooms. Working knowledge of a Housing Software. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.   Salary Range $73,899.90-$88,673.69 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Residential Support Services Position Type Professional - Non-Faculty Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Building-Maintenance-Worker_R1004657": {
      "title": "Building Maintenance Worker (Housekeeper) (Multiple Positions)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Crew Supervisor and/or Assistant Housekeeping Supervisor, the Building Maintenance Worker is responsible for maintaining cleanliness of the Montclair State University Facilities. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Clean campus facilities alone or in teams; clean public areas and meeting spaces. Perform room set-ups; replace light bulbs, clean light fixtures and restrooms. Sweep, mop, strip and wax, buff floors; vacuum and shampoo carpets. Collect and remove trash, bring trash to curb or receptacles, transfer recyclable materials. Dust all surface and vent, and clean inside window surfaces. Clean desks, tables, chairs, and remove graffiti. Clean offices, classrooms, and work areas. Perform snow removal as directed. Attend in-service training and participate in University quality and processing improvement initiatives. Assist with the sorting, distribution, transportation and storage of cleaning supplies. Keep janitorial closet stocked and clean; maintain housekeeping equipment. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : Ability to speak, read, and understand English. Ability to lift 25 lbs. and use a ladder. Ability to work any shift, overtime and holidays in the performance of assigned responsibilities. PREFERRED : A high school diploma or its equivalency. Housekeeping experience in a university, school or hospital setting. *NOTE: This is a Civil Service position.  As required by the State of New Jersey, in order to be certified to the position and attain permanent status in title, candidates are required to successfully serve a 4-Month Working Test Period. This position is designated as essential. The designation of essential requires employees at these 24/7 facilities to be present due to inclement weather situations. This position requires on campus work and is not a position that allows remote work.         SALARY RANGE: O09: $38,640.95 - $55,447.65 *NOTE: Salaries for internal candidates are determined by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission’s formula. Salaries for external candidates are determined up to step four, $43,682.96. NJ SAME Applicants This position is a non-competitive, unclassified posting and complies with the NJ SAME Program. If you are applying under the New Jersey \"SAME\" program, your supporting documents (Schedule A or B letter), resume (CV), as well as the names and contact information for three professional references should also be sent to: same@montclair.edu and hrcompliance@montclair.edu For more information on the SAME program visit their website at: https://nj.gov/csc/same/overview/index.shtml , email: SAME@csc.nj.gov , or call CSC at: 833-691-0404. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act P.L. 2011 c.70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees in certain positions (other than faculty who are exempt) are required to obtain New Jersey residency within one (1) year of employment. Applicants who have a concern with meeting this requirement should discuss with Human Resources if the position for which they have applied is eligible for an exemption from this requirement. Salary Range $18.58-$26.66 Hourly The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Housekeeping Services/Acad. 4 Position Type Services Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
