    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Assignment-Coordinator_R1004988": {
      "title": "Newsroom Assignment Coordinator (NJ PBS)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the News Director, the Assignment Coordinator is the real-time nerve center of the NJ PBS newsroom, managing the daily assignment workflow. The Assignment Coordinator coordinates crew and equipment assignments, monitors police/fire scanners and social media for breaking news, and maintains journalist and photographer scheduling. In addition, this position develops and maintains news relationships, contacts and sources, gathers editorial information on breaking news and developing stories, books interviews and guests for programs and platforms, manages planning for future story and events coverage, and serves as a central communication hub between the News Director, anchor, reporters, producers, photojournalists, and editors.  PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Monitor social media and wire services for breaking news and developing stories. Assign reporters and photojournalists to stories based on availability, location, and editorial priorities. Manage crew scheduling and equipment deployment, ensuring adequate coverage for all assigned stories. Maintain the assignment log and daily story list, updating it throughout the day as stories develop. Ensure that all platforms are considered when making story assignments, shooting news coverage, and producing content to maximize the value of the material gathered for all platforms. Communicate with field crews via phone and two-way radio, relaying updates and coordinating logistics. Coordinate live shot logistics, including satellite truck positioning, microwave paths, and IP-based live connections. Assist producers with rundown planning by providing real-time updates on story status and crew availability. Maintain contact databases for emergency services, government offices, and community organizations. Contribute ideas and story pitches to editorial meetings. Develop and maintain news contacts and sources. Manage planning for future story and events coverage. Monitor competitor content and flag gaps in coverage. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. Perform other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS:  REQUIRED: A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in a related field. At least three years of demonstrated assignment desk experience in broadcast or digital daily newsroom operations, including managing breaking news. including crew scheduling and assignment coordination. Strong news judgment. Ability to manage multiple concurrent field assignments in a live news environment. Valid driver’s license. PREFERRED: Master’s degree from an accredited college or university in a related field. Prior assignment desk experience at a television or digital daily news organization. Knowledge of New Jersey geography, government, and public safety agencies. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY: Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.   Salary Range $75,000.00-$85,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Technical-Manager--Workday-Systems_R1004844": {
      "title": "Technical Manager, Workday Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY : Reporting to the Assistant Vice President, Workday Systems, the Technical Manager, Workday Systems is responsible for leading and supporting the technical architecture, integrations, data management, and system configuration across Workday Student, Human Capital Management (HCM), and Financial Management modules. This role partners closely with functional stakeholders, IT leadership, and vendors to ensure secure, scalable, and high-performing Workday solutions that align with organizational goals. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES :  Serve as the technical lead for Workday Student, HCM, and Finance platforms. Define and maintain Workday technical architecture, standards, and best practices. Manage and provide technical guidance to Workday Technical Developers. Oversee design, development, and support Workday integrations using EIBs, Core Connectors, Studio, APIs, and third-party middleware. Manage inbound and outbound data flows with external systems (e.g. Student systems, Payroll, Benefit providers, Banking, Reporting tools, LMS). Leverage Workday Extend to design, build, and govern custom applications that integrate seamlessly with Workday Student, HCM, and Financial Management Ensure data integrity, security, and compliance across all Workday modules. Support reporting, calculated fields, and advanced analytics as needed. Coordinate work with implementation partners and third-party vendors. Manage technical project deliverables, timelines, and documentation. Partner with functional leads to translate business requirements into technical solutions. Support Workday releases, testing, and deployment activities (bi-annual updates). Troubleshoot complex technical issues and provide escalation support. Coordinate planning, execution, and communication for Enterprise Systems initiatives. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED :  Bachelor’s degree in Information Systems, Computer Science, or a related field. Minimum of five years of experience supporting Workday in a technical capacity. Demonstrated expertise in: Workday integrations (EIB, Core Connectors, Studio, APIs) Calculated fields and reporting Dashboards Minimum of two years of experience leading technical teams or acting as a technical lead. Excellent communication skills with the ability to work across technical and non-technical stakeholders. Strong leadership skills, and an understanding of higher education and/or complex enterprise environments. PREFERRED : Experience in Higher Education Experience with Workday Student   Workday certifications (Integration, HCM, Financials, or Student). Hands on experience with Workday Extend Experience with Identity Management Systems This is a hybrid position requiring candidate to be onsite 3 days per week. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instruction. Salary Range $140,000.00-$160,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department Workday Applications Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Reporter--North-Jersey_R1004984": {
      "title": "Reporter, North Jersey",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY Reporting to the News Director, the Reporter, North Jersey, covers news, politics, and community affairs in northern New Jersey, including Bergen, Essex, Passaic, Hudson, Morris, Warren, and Sussex counties. This position develops and pitches original stories, shoots and edits video packages, conducts interviews, and files content for broadcast, streaming, and digital platforms. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Develop and pitch story ideas from the northern New Jersey beat. Conduct on-camera and off-camera interviews with sources, officials, and community members. Shoot, write, and edit video packages for broadcast and digital delivery. File content for daily newscasts and digital platforms on deadline. Cover breaking news, government meetings, community events, and enterprise stories. Cultivate and maintain source relationships with officials, community leaders, and organizations across the coverage area. Contribute to digital and social media content, including short-form video and social posts. Contribute to the booking of guests and interview subjects. Collaborate with producers and editors on story development and editorial priorities. Experience with digital and social media storytelling. May substitute-anchor on news programs from time to time as needed. Represent NJ PBS at community events in the northern New Jersey coverage area. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED: A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in journalism, communications, broadcasting, or a related field.  A minimum of three years of video-based reporting experience including field reporting, and clip and package production. Ability to shoot and edit video content for broadcast and digital delivery. Valid NJ driver’s license. Experience with digital and social media storytelling. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. PREFERRED: Knowledge of northern New Jersey communities, institutions, and government. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. PROCEDURE FOR CANDIDACY Applicants should include a resume and cover letter describing how their background, skills and education match the needs of the University. When applying, please take a moment to carefully read and follow the steps in the application instructions.  Salary Range $70,000.00-$85,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
    },
    "https://montclair.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Montclair-NJ/Reporter--South-Jersey_R1004986": {
      "title": "Reporter, South Jersey",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nIMPORTANT APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Upload Resume or Curriculum Vitae for automatic population of information to the application. The contact information, work experience, and education listed on your Resume/CV will be parsed and input into your Montclair application. Review information and double-check all fields containing information that the system parsed – the software is intelligent, but you need to verify that the data is accurate. In the “My Experience” section, you will find a Resume/CV upload option where you can submit your cover letter and all other supporting documents. Note: If you have an expansive CV, we recommend that you apply manually and only include the positions you have held in the last ten (10) years . You will then be able to attach your Resume/CV, as well as all other supporting documentation in the \"My Experience\" section of your application. Job Description SUMMARY: Reporting to the News Director, the Reporter, South Jersey covers news, communities, and affairs in southern New Jersey, including Camden, Burlington, Ocean, Atlantic, Cape May, Cumberland, Salem, and Gloucester counties. This individual develops original stories reflecting the distinct character and concerns of South Jersey communities and files content for broadcast, streaming, and digital platforms. PRINCIPAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Develop and pitch story ideas from the South Jersey beat. Conduct on-camera and off-camera interviews with sources, officials, and community members. Shoot, write, and edit video packages for broadcast and digital delivery. File content for daily newscasts and digital platforms on deadline. Cover breaking news, government meetings, community events, and enterprise stories across the coverage area. Cultivate source relationships with officials, community leaders, and organizations in South Jersey. Contribute to digital and social media content, including short-form video and social posts. Collaborate with producers and editors on story development and editorial priorities. Contribute to the booking of guests and interview subjects. May substitute-anchor on news programs from time to time as needed. Represent NJ PBS at community events in the South Jersey coverage area. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. Performs other duties as assigned. Management retains the right to add or change job duties at any time. QUALIFICATIONS:  REQUIRED: A Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in journalism, communications, broadcasting, or a related field.  A minimum of three years of video-based reporting experience, including field reporting, and clip and package production. Ability to shoot and edit video content for broadcast and digital delivery. Valid NJ driver’s license. Experience with digital and social media storytelling. Adhere to NJ PBS editorial standards and public media ethics guidelines. PREFERRED: Knowledge of South Jersey communities, institutions, and regional issues. Bilingual proficiency in English and Spanish. Salary Range $70,000.00-$85,000.00 Annually The position may also be eligible for comprehensive benefits, including health insurance, retirement plans, and tuition assistance. For further details, please visit:  https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/benefits/     Montclair State University considers factors such as, but not limited to, scope and responsibilities of the position, candidate’s relevant work experience, education, skills, and internal equity, when extending an offer. Salary offers for internal employees who are part of a collective bargaining unit (CBU) and are applying to a position that is within a CBU will be determined in accordance with contractual provisions.  Department NJ PBS Position Type Administrative Contact Information: For questions or concerns, please contact Human Resources' Workday Recruiting Support at 973-655-5000 (Option 2) , or email talent@montclair.edu . Inclusion Statement Montclair State University values access and educational excellence. We are committed to an environment of diverse perspectives which ensures that graduates will be civically engaged, committed to democracy, and prepared to thrive as global citizens. We foster a community that promotes varied experiences and voices. We seek applicants who will contribute diverse ideas and perspectives and who value an environment that promotes educational growth and advancement for all. EEO/AA Statement Montclair State University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action institution with a strong commitment to diversity. Additional information can be found on the website at   www.montclair.edu/human-resources/about-us/eo-aa-and-diversity/ Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 Policy Montclair State is required by Title IX and 34 C.F.R. 106 not to discriminate on the basis of sex or gender, and does not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities.  The requirement to not discriminate on the basis of sex or gender in the operation of education programs and activities extends to admission and employment. For further details, please visit: https://www.montclair.edu/human-resources/job-seekers/"
